<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113342" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χᾰραδρ-όομαι</span></b> , 
			Pass.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be broken into
				clefts by mountain-streams, to be full of gullies,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χώρη κεχαραδρωμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.25
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς ἂν χαραδρωθείη ὁ χῶρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.176
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ πόροι
			χαραδροῦνται</span> the pores <i>are widened into large
				channels,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Flat.</u>
				10
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
